    "created_at": "2026-09-25T09:28:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-25T09:28:41Z",
    "body": "Yeah Claude also noticed that this exposes an issue with `frame`:\r\n\r\n> - source:108829–108833: this PR makes frame reach \"run the iframe load event steps given targetNavigable's container\".\r\n> - Why: \"iframe load event steps\" (source:35698) takes an iframe element and reads its pending resource-timing start time and URL, which only iframes have (source:35791 ff.). On main a frame never got here, because its initialInsertion sat in the\r\n      srcdocString slot. With this PR, an inserted <frame src=\"javascript:undefined\"> passes the check and gets those iframe steps.\r\n> - Should frames fire load at all? Yes. WebKit uses one path for both elements (FrameLoader::executeJavaScriptURL → LocalDOMWindow::dispatchLoadEvent → dispatchLoadEventToParent).\r\n> - Fix: branch the way \"completely finish loading\" does (source:114118–114125): if the container is an iframe, run the iframe load event steps; otherwise fire an event named load at it. The frame about:blank branch already does the same\r\n      (source:155315–155316).\r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
